codex
Implemented REL-1e flag-gated promotion.

Summary:
- Added `DISCO_HOST_VERIFY_AUTHORITATIVE` via `disco_env`, default off.
- Host verifier becomes authoritative only when enabled: pass proceeds, fail refuses with a loud system reminder and bounded `unverified_release`.
- Browser inline self-verify delegates/skips when host authoritative verification is available.
- Prompt self-verify mandate is softened only when the flag is enabled.
- Non-app/files handoffs without a validator record `verdict="unverifiable"` and `verified=false`.
- Added focused REL-1e tests plus manifest-stamp coverage.

Verification:
- `git diff --check` passed.
- `.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest packages/core -m "not integration" -q -k "verif or finish or shadow"` passed.
- Focused REL-1e/shadow/canary tests passed: `16 passed`.

The exact requested package gate was attempted, but it did not complete because existing agent-server selected tests hang in teardown/order. Notably, `test_artifact_route.py::test_finished_run_falls_back_to_snapshot` hangs alone, and `test_build_surface.py::test_request_plan_after_finish_reopens_plan_mode_with_a_new_revision` prints a pass dot then does not exit. I did not restart servers or commit.

